scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: jazz-legends
run_id: 2
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The config
    implementation uses fallback-to-default pattern without distinguishing NotFound
    from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209 protection on ServerError Display \u2014 reviewer\
    \ verified: 'body is stored but not shown in format!(\"{err}\")'. Security tests\
    \ include CWE-209 error exposure tests. However, the stderr eprintln leaking was\
    \ not fully addressed \u2014 reviewer did not flag the remaining Display impls\
    \ leaking to stderr."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests in siem_client.rs (19 tests) and security.rs\
    \ (CWE-113 newline validation). Dev implemented CWE-113 newline validation in\
    \ client.rs:28-40. However, the deeper issue of using raw String instead of TenantId\
    \ from axiathon-core was not caught \u2014 only the symptom (CRLF injection) was\
    \ addressed, not the type-safety root cause."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Dev added 6 dependencies with direct version strings instead of workspace
    = true. Reviewer flagged the toml version mismatch but did not flag the missing
    workspace = true pattern for the other dependencies.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: ''ConfigFile and ServerSection accept unknown
    fields silently (config.rs:4-13)... Adding #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] would
    catch configuration errors early. A user who typos timout = 30 or adds tokn =
    "secret" gets no warning.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (assert! with
    is_none() || ...). The test was written by TEA and passed through Dev and Reviewer
    without the logical flaw being caught.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test (let _ = config with no assert_eq!
    checks). The test was written by TEA and not flagged by Reviewer.
